-- title:
--   Original finitecap two-grid Gaussian reward and time coefficient L2 integrability package
-- statement:
--   The actual original stopped finite-cap Gaussian grid reward L_m and the original two step coefficient fields K_m have integrable squares and cross products, both for each time and after integrating time on (0,n). This finite-horizon L2 package follows from predictable finite-cell L2 bounds and the clipped gradient bound.
-- source:
--   Necessary unproved physical-integrability hypothesis for original finitecap double Gaussian polarisation gbB68 (6cb63bc4-12e8-41cb-933c-19ad50327bbc). Proved inputs include gbB57 cell MemLp, gbB64 clipped coefficient uniform bound, and gbB59 measurable adapted coefficients. The bridge from this package to gbB68 uses Proved gb73 and newly published gb91.

